[{"id":4,"title":"test: add empty-input and blank-line tests","state":"merged","author":"priya-learns","opened_at":"2026-06-10","merged_at":"2026-06-10","linked_issue":null,"branch":"test/empty-input","description":"Adds two missing tests:\n- `test_empty_input` — confirms `render('')` returns `''`\n- `test_blank_lines_ignored` — confirms blank lines between blocks don't produce output\n\nNo linked issue. I noticed these cases weren't covered while reading through the test file.\n\n**Changes:**\n- `tests/test_mdlite.py`: 2 test functions added\n\n**Testing:**\n- All existing tests still pass\n- Both new tests pass","diff_summary":"tests/test_mdlite.py: added test_empty_input and test_blank_lines_ignored","review_comments":[{"author":"riya-dev","date":"2026-06-10","body":"Nice addition — these edge cases should definitely be covered. Merging.","resolved":true}],"lesson":"good_newcomer_pr","lesson_note":"No linked issue, no bug to fix — just a contributor who read the test file, noticed a gap, and filled it cleanly. Small scope, passes CI, maintainer merged same day. You don't need a bug report to make a useful contribution."},{"id":7,"title":"fix: strip trailing spaces from headings","state":"merged","author":"dev-rohan","opened_at":"2026-08-25","merged_at":"2026-08-28","linked_issue":null,"branch":"fix/trailing-spaces","description":"Headings with trailing spaces produce output like `<h1>Hello   </h1>`. This strips them.\n\n**Changes:**\n- `src/mdlite.py`: `.rstrip()` added to the text slice in each heading branch\n\n**Testing:**\n- Added `test_heading_trailing_space` in `tests/test_mdlite.py`\n- All existing tests pass","diff_summary":"src/mdlite.py: changed line[2:] to line[2:].rstrip() (and equivalents for h2, h3)","review_comments":[{"author":"ci-bot","date":"2026-08-25","body":"`black --check` failed on `src/mdlite.py`. Please run `black src/ tests/` before pushing.","resolved":true},{"author":"riya-dev","date":"2026-08-26","body":"The change looks correct but CI is red. Can you run `black src/ tests/` and push the result?","resolved":true},{"author":"dev-rohan","date":"2026-08-27","body":"Done — pushed a formatting commit. CI is green now.","resolved":true},{"author":"riya-dev","date":"2026-08-28","body":"Perfect. Clean diff, test included, CI passing. Merging — thanks!","resolved":true}],"lesson":"polite_review_response","lesson_note":"CI failed on the first push because of formatting. The maintainer didn't reject the PR — they asked for one specific fix. The contributor ran black, pushed the result, and the PR merged cleanly. A CI failure on your first push is normal; what matters is how you respond to it."},{"id":9,"title":"docs: fix typo in README import example","state":"open","author":"priya-learns","opened_at":"2026-09-12","merged_at":null,"linked_issue":8,"branch":"docs/readme-typo","description":"Fixes #8.\n\nThe usage example in README.md says `form src.mdlite import render` — changed to `from`.\n\n**Changes:**\n- `README.md`: one word corrected in the usage example\n\n**Draft:** still checking the rest of the README for other issues before marking ready.","diff_summary":"README.md: changed 'form src.mdlite import render' to 'from src.mdlite import render'","review_comments":[],"lesson":null,"lesson_note":"Draft PR opened by a contributor who claimed issue #8. Still in progress — no review yet."}]